Host-side control-flow regression harness for the whole-run corrupt-save
notice: GameActivity::onEnter() finds GAME_STATE.hasSaveFile() true but
GAME_STATE.loadFromFile() false (a present-but-unloadable save.bin), lands in
the CorruptSaveNotice/WholeRun modal, and a scripted Confirm button release
drives the real loop() into GameActivity::resolveWholeRunCorruptNotice().
There is a single Continue outcome now (Stuart's locked spec, msg 3940) --
no selection, no purge branch -- Confirm and Back both resolve identically.
Not a gtest suite (see test/README for those) -- this compiles the REAL,
unmodified Activity.cpp/GameActivity.cpp against the REAL GameState.cpp/
GameSave.cpp/DungeonGenerator.cpp/AchievementBus.cpp/FlavorText.cpp, so the
resolve path is proven against shipped code, not a transcription of it.

This is a LOGIC/control-flow test, not a pixel-rendering test: GfxRenderer
and GameRenderer are stubbed (fast-compiling fakes), unlike the
test/sponsor_hp_clamp/ precedent, which links the real GameRenderer for a
different (HUD-value) purpose. Nothing here ever draws a frame.

Same standalone-g++, symlinked-mirror-with-shadow-headers technique as
test/game_title_render/ -- see that README's "Why mirror/ exists" section
for the general explanation.

## Why the private state is never read directly

screenMode / corruptNoticeScope are private on GameActivity with no
accessor, and per this project's precedent (test/sponsor_hp_clamp/), a
friend/accessor is avoided rather than added just for a test. This harness
instead asserts only through observable PUBLIC side effects:
  - GAME_STATE.hasSaveFile() / Storage.exists(...) before and after Confirm,
    to prove save.bin was left untouched (there is no purge branch anymore --
    Stuart's locked spec, msg 3940).
  - GAME_STATE.player.{turnCount,hp,maxHp,dungeonDepth} after Confirm, to
    prove GAME_STATE.newGame() ran and produced fresh state.
  - A second harmless loop() call staying stable, as the strongest available
    proof screenMode flipped back to Playing (a stuck CorruptSaveNotice modal
    would still re-run resolveWholeRunCorruptNotice() on another Confirm
    release instead of being a no-op).

If a future change makes any of this genuinely unprovable indirectly, add a
narrowly-scoped test-only accessor rather than reaching further into
private internals with tricks (see the task-level instruction this harness
was built under).

## Build

  INCLUDES="-include Arduino.h \
    -I test/whole_run_corrupt_save/stubs \
    -I test/whole_run_corrupt_save/mirror/src \
    -I test/whole_run_corrupt_save/mirror/src/activities \
    -I test/whole_run_corrupt_save/mirror/src/activities/game \
    -I src -I src/game \
    -I lib/Serialization -I lib/Memory"

  mkdir -p test/whole_run_corrupt_save/build
  for f in \
      test/whole_run_corrupt_save/WholeRunCorruptSaveHarness.cpp \
      test/whole_run_corrupt_save/mirror/src/activities/Activity.cpp \
      test/whole_run_corrupt_save/mirror/src/activities/game/GameActivity.cpp \
      src/game/GameState.cpp \
      src/game/GameSave.cpp \
      src/game/DungeonGenerator.cpp \
      src/game/AchievementBus.cpp \
      src/game/FlavorText.cpp; do
    g++ -std=c++20 -O0 -Wall -Wextra $INCLUDES -c "$f" \
      -o "test/whole_run_corrupt_save/build/$(basename $f .cpp).o"
  done
  g++ test/whole_run_corrupt_save/build/*.o \
    -o test/whole_run_corrupt_save/build/whole_run_corrupt_save_harness

  ./test/whole_run_corrupt_save/build/whole_run_corrupt_save_harness

`-include Arduino.h` is required (not just an -I stub dir) because
GameActivity.cpp calls millis() with no explicit #include of its own --
on the real ESP32 Arduino toolchain, Arduino.h is force-included globally
via the build system, and this harness replicates that with -include
rather than editing the real .cpp to add a header it doesn't itself declare.

## Notable stub-placement gotcha

GameActivity.h does `#include "game/GameRenderer.h"` (not a bare
"GameRenderer.h") -- the stub must live at stubs/game/GameRenderer.h, not
stubs/GameRenderer.h, or g++'s quoted-include search resolves straight
through to the real src/game/GameRenderer.h via the -I src/game path
instead of ever reaching the stub, silently pulling in the full font/EPD
pipeline this harness deliberately avoids. Caught only at link time
(undefined references to the stub's inert bodies, because the real
GameRenderer.cpp was never compiled in) -- worth remembering before adding
any other stub whose real header is included via a "subdir/Name.h" path.

## Output

Fully deterministic: a fresh stub-filesystem save.bin is hand-written with
version byte 0xFF (guaranteed to mismatch SAVE_FILE_VERSION, no dependency
on knowing its current value) every run, and the stub SD root under
test/whole_run_corrupt_save/build/fake_sd is wiped at the start of main().
PASS prints all assertions passed and exits 0; any failed CHECK() prints to
stderr, the run still completes, and main() exits 1.
